.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-HASH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-hash
.Nd print or check SHA-2, SHA-3 and SHAKE digests of files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis hash
.Op Fl a Ar hash
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm noqtis hash
.Op Fl a Ar hash
.Fl c | Fl -check
.Op Ar list ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis hash
prints one line per
.Ar file
in the format of
.Xr sha256sum 1 :
the digest in lower-case hex, two spaces and the name.
A name that holds a backslash, a line feed or a carriage return is written
with
.Ql \e\e ,
.Ql \en
and
.Ql \er ,
and the line starts with a backslash, as
.Xr sha256sum 1
does.
With no
.Ar file ,
or with
.Ql - ,
it reads standard input.
.Pp
With
.Fl c ,
each argument is a
.Ar list
of such lines (standard input when there is none).
For every line it prints
.Ql <name>: OK ,
.Ql <name>: FAILED
or
.Ql <name>: FAILED open or read .
A line may mark binary mode with
.Ql *
before the name, as
.Xr sha256sum 1
writes it; noqtis always reads files as bytes.
Empty lines are skipped; any other line that is not a digest of the chosen
hash is reported with its line number.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a Ar hash , Fl -alg Ns = Ns Ar hash
One of
.Cm sha224 , sha256
(the default),
.Cm sha384 , sha512 , sha512-224 , sha512-256 ,
.Cm sha3-224 , sha3-256 , sha3-384 , sha3-512 ,
.Cm shake128
(32 bytes of output) and
.Cm shake256
(64 bytes).
With
.Fl c ,
every line of the lists must use this hash.
.It Fl c , Fl -check
Check digests instead of printing them.
A listed name that is not a regular file (a folder, a FIFO, a device)
fails without being opened.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
Every digest was printed, or every line checked.
.It 1
With
.Fl c :
a digest differs, a listed file cannot be read, a line is malformed, or no
line was found.
.It 2
A usage error or an unknown hash, a
.Ar file
or
.Ar list
that cannot be read, or standard output that cannot be written.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ printf 'abc' > abc.txt
$ noqtis hash abc.txt
ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad  abc.txt
$ noqtis hash -a sha3-256 abc.txt > SUMS
$ noqtis hash -a sha3-256 -c SUMS
abc.txt: OK
.Ed
.Pp
Checking digests made by
.Xr sha256sum 1 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ sha256sum abc.txt | noqtis hash -c
abc.txt: OK
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr sha256sum 1 ,
.Xr nqhash 3
